  "notes": "Entirely business-type entity (community college); College column used, Foundation (discrete component) column excluded. Receipts = operating revenues plus positive nonoperating revenues; no single printed total, so totals computed (see reported_totals). Capital debt interest expense shown as a disbursement. Capital appropriations 22,523,578 and loss on disposal (322,647) recorded in business_type.other_financing. Statement lists expenses by object only; each object line takes the dominant function for that object in the General Fund expenditure schedule (p4): personnel and operating expenses support services, travel instruction (review). Retainage payable categorized as accounts payable; noncurrent compensated absences as accrued liabilities. Deferred inflows 279,275 put in deferred_inflows list. Detail: General Fund expenditure schedule is the only schedule; personnel services include benefits. Trimmed PDF has 4 pages (statement pages 18, 19, 20, 49). Read pages 1-4 of 4",
  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "Capital appropriations of 22,523,578 (printed under Other revenues, below income before other revenues) are recorded with the loss on disposal (322,647) as business-type other financing, not receipts. The cash flow statement (p3) shows 20,973,105 of 'Property taxes - capital improvement fund', so this is capital-levy property tax. Should it count as property tax receipts instead?",
      "amount": 22523578,
